WEBVTT

00:00:31.570 --> 00:00:33.900
Guards! The enemy's upon us!

00:00:37.280 --> 00:00:38.910
Call off your men.

00:00:38.910 --> 00:00:41.620
I'm not here to fight, my lord.

00:00:41.620 --> 00:00:43.160
What nonsense is this?!

00:00:43.160 --> 00:00:46.750
My son is dead because of you,

00:00:46.750 --> 00:00:49.590
Wein Salema Arbalest!

00:00:49.590 --> 00:00:51.090
Well, now.

00:00:51.090 --> 00:00:54.970
Do you seek bloodshed before
the remains of your noble son?

00:00:55.970 --> 00:00:57.300
Marquess Antgadull,

00:00:57.300 --> 00:01:03.220
should we not sit down and speak
about this... for both of our sakes?

00:01:05.270 --> 00:01:07.900
The Natran prince wormed
his way into manor?!

00:01:07.900 --> 00:01:08.940
How many?!

00:01:08.940 --> 00:01:09.940
Five in all.

00:01:09.940 --> 00:01:11.730
There are only five?

00:01:11.730 --> 00:01:14.320
How many men do we have at the ready?

00:01:14.320 --> 00:01:15.950
As many as ten.

00:01:15.950 --> 00:01:17.610
Assemble them all now!

00:01:17.610 --> 00:01:18.700
Yes, sir!

00:01:18.700 --> 00:01:22.620
I can't let the Natran prince
seize the initiative.

00:01:22.620 --> 00:01:25.410
I must deal with this here and now!

00:01:31.380 --> 00:01:34.590
I'll get straight to the point,
Marquess Antgadull.

00:01:34.590 --> 00:01:37.760
Her Imperial Highness knows everything.

00:01:41.600 --> 00:01:44.720
And what precisely do you mean by that?

00:01:44.720 --> 00:01:49.480
Of course, I'm referring to my lord's
involvement in the rebellion plot.

00:01:49.480 --> 00:01:51.860
What?!

00:01:51.860 --> 00:01:53.570
I must warn you.

00:01:53.570 --> 00:01:56.700
The time for denial is long past.

00:01:56.700 --> 00:02:01.370
And if you were to kill me now,
you'd eventually be brought to justice.

00:02:01.370 --> 00:02:05.410
Wh-What nonsense is this? I would never...

00:02:05.410 --> 00:02:09.000
You're up to something!
Tell me why you've come here!

00:02:09.000 --> 00:02:11.790
It is to pronounce a
death sentence upon me?!

00:02:11.790 --> 00:02:14.880
There's no reason to panic, my lord.

00:02:14.880 --> 00:02:19.930
After all, Lord Geralt,
the root of all this evil, is dead.

00:02:22.800 --> 00:02:27.270
What a terrible tale!
A truly terrible tale!

00:02:27.270 --> 00:02:32.610
Abandoning his allegiance to the empire,
he took his own father captive

00:02:32.610 --> 00:02:36.900
and seized upon the rebellion's
chaos to seek independence!

00:02:36.900 --> 00:02:39.610
D-Don't tell me...

00:02:39.610 --> 00:02:43.070
...you intend to pin this
whole thing on Geralt?!

00:04:15.790 --> 00:04:19.340
It's a classic case of
a wolf in sheep's clothing!

00:04:19.340 --> 00:04:22.760
Considering Geralt's poor
reputation throughout the empire,

00:04:22.760 --> 00:04:26.260
I imagine most will accept this as fact.

00:04:26.260 --> 00:04:29.890
My lord may even find
they sympathize with you.

00:04:29.890 --> 00:04:33.560
In any case, the rat was sniffed out

00:04:33.560 --> 00:04:37.980
and caught in a trap thanks to
Her Highness Princess Lowellmina.

00:04:37.980 --> 00:04:40.480
Her genius is truly a marvel.

00:04:40.480 --> 00:04:44.780
Of course, my lord will likely
be accused of treason.

00:04:44.780 --> 00:04:49.280
After all, a father must
atone for his son's sins.

00:04:49.280 --> 00:04:53.200
But if you hand over all evidence
about the rebellion plot

00:04:53.200 --> 00:04:55.540
and testify regarding your involvement,

00:04:55.540 --> 00:05:01.050
Her Highness assured me you'll suffer
no more than a reduction in domain income.

00:05:01.050 --> 00:05:03.420
It couldn't have been helped.

00:05:03.420 --> 00:05:05.260
My lord is a victim.

00:05:05.260 --> 00:05:06.840
Her Highness awaits in Natra.

00:05:06.840 --> 00:05:11.600
Will you not swallow your pride
and throw yourself upon her mercy?

00:05:11.600 --> 00:05:14.480
The fate of House Antgadull
is in your hands.

00:05:14.480 --> 00:05:18.100
Does this not call for an astute decision?

00:05:19.690 --> 00:05:23.110
Come on, take the bait!

00:05:28.570 --> 00:05:33.330
I-I shall prepare to leave.

00:05:33.330 --> 00:05:35.660
But I'll need a little time.

00:05:35.660 --> 00:05:38.040
Oh, yeah!

00:05:40.960 --> 00:05:43.880
My lord has made a most wise choice.

00:05:43.880 --> 00:05:46.800
It should all be downhill from here.

00:05:55.980 --> 00:05:58.770
The inn should be just a bit farther.

00:05:58.770 --> 00:06:02.690
Grinahae accepted your proposal,
but was that really the best outcome?

00:06:02.690 --> 00:06:05.070
He also asked to delay
the departure till tomorrow.

00:06:05.070 --> 00:06:08.110
His indecisiveness is a given.

00:06:08.110 --> 00:06:12.160
Well, I suppose we'll just have to wait.

00:06:12.160 --> 00:06:13.280
Your Highness!

00:06:13.280 --> 00:06:17.120
Yes, it <i>is </i>awfully quiet.

00:06:17.120 --> 00:06:20.710
They're watching us
and have us surrounded.

00:06:20.710 --> 00:06:23.340
Or thereabout.
They're on that side street, too.

00:06:23.340 --> 00:06:26.170
A well-laid plan.

00:06:26.170 --> 00:06:28.300
We'll cut our way out.

00:06:28.300 --> 00:06:29.930
Try to keep up!

00:06:29.930 --> 00:06:31.850
Oh, I will.

00:06:31.850 --> 00:06:32.970
Let's do this!

00:06:37.680 --> 00:06:41.190
You were a fool to the end, my son.

00:06:41.190 --> 00:06:44.070
But it is only natural.

00:06:44.070 --> 00:06:46.570
For you were mine.

00:06:52.160 --> 00:06:56.580
In the end at least,
I shall fulfill my fatherly duty.

00:06:56.580 --> 00:06:58.960
Let this be a tribute to Geralt.

00:06:58.960 --> 00:07:03.750
The troops have mustered?
Don't neglect to notify the checkpoints!

00:07:03.750 --> 00:07:08.550
We shall capture the Natran Prince
and seize Princess Lowellmina!

00:07:13.140 --> 00:07:18.480
They knew which way we were going,
cleared the streets, and set up an ambush.

00:07:18.480 --> 00:07:20.560
These aren't Grinahae's men.

00:07:20.560 --> 00:07:22.350
Then whose?

00:07:23.480 --> 00:07:28.320
It won't be long before the town guards
hear the fighting and come running.

00:07:28.320 --> 00:07:31.650
So whoever is doing this
is banking on a short battle.

00:07:31.650 --> 00:07:36.240
That they've led us here means
there's a trap near at hand.

00:07:40.000 --> 00:07:41.290
Damn it.

00:07:45.000 --> 00:07:48.380
I thought I had you.
It seems luck is on your side.

00:07:48.380 --> 00:07:50.550
Did that look like luck to you?

00:07:50.550 --> 00:07:54.140
We've never met, but I'd say
you need your eyes examined.

00:07:54.140 --> 00:07:55.640
That was <i>way </i>too close!

00:07:55.640 --> 00:07:59.060
I could never repeat that move,
even to save my life!

00:07:59.060 --> 00:08:01.890
He knows what he's doing.
Not a single opening.

00:08:01.890 --> 00:08:03.060
That leaves...

00:08:03.060 --> 00:08:04.350
Now I see.

00:08:04.350 --> 00:08:09.570
You're the ones who sucked Marquess
Antgadull into the rebellion plot.

00:08:09.570 --> 00:08:13.990
Of course, you'll never admit to it,
so I'll take a guess.

00:08:13.990 --> 00:08:17.080
You and your people are...

00:08:17.080 --> 00:08:19.620
...spies from the west.

00:08:22.710 --> 00:08:26.500
Involving a backwater marquess
in your plot was quite pigheaded.

00:08:26.500 --> 00:08:28.500
But you barked up the wrong tree.

00:08:28.500 --> 00:08:31.970
And it's left your plot in tatters.

00:08:31.970 --> 00:08:35.340
Well, that look says you
think you may yet salvage it.

00:08:35.340 --> 00:08:38.890
I imagine you still have
comrades here in town.

00:08:38.890 --> 00:08:43.850
But they are busy elsewhere,
or am I wrong?

00:08:43.850 --> 00:08:47.860
Their mission is to
silence Marquess Antgadull.

00:08:47.860 --> 00:08:49.770
First, they'll assassinate him!

00:08:49.770 --> 00:08:54.200
Then they'll burn down his manor
to destroy all evidence of your plot!

00:08:54.200 --> 00:08:55.950
He has...!

00:08:55.950 --> 00:09:00.040
He's spied on us the whole time?!
Is that how he read our every move?

00:09:00.040 --> 00:09:02.500
But that's all he has. No need to panic.

00:09:02.500 --> 00:09:04.960
It doesn't matter if he knows.

00:09:04.960 --> 00:09:07.710
Our men have already
slipped into the manor.

00:09:07.710 --> 00:09:10.210
If I just take out Wein
and his guards here...

00:09:10.210 --> 00:09:13.970
Did you really think <i>all</i>
my men were here with me?

00:09:17.590 --> 00:09:18.600
Hurry!

00:09:18.600 --> 00:09:20.310
We start with the documents.

00:09:20.310 --> 00:09:22.810
Isn't that room off-limits?

00:09:25.480 --> 00:09:26.730
Crap.

00:09:37.990 --> 00:09:40.450
Wh-Who the hell are you?

00:09:42.200 --> 00:09:46.750
Take this, and slip into the manor
by claiming to be his squire.

00:09:46.750 --> 00:09:49.040
Grinahae will be assassinated?

00:09:49.040 --> 00:09:54.210
Yes, I want you to save him
and secure proof of the rebellion.

00:09:54.210 --> 00:09:56.510
You make it sound easy.

00:09:56.510 --> 00:09:58.090
It <i>is </i>easy,

00:09:58.090 --> 00:09:59.890
for you at least, Nanaki.

00:10:05.310 --> 00:10:07.640
Who <i>are </i>you?

00:10:07.640 --> 00:10:11.480
Isn't it obvious? I'm the competition.

00:10:14.980 --> 00:10:18.860
I bet Wein's fighting for
his life right about now.

00:10:24.080 --> 00:10:27.160
So you already have men in the manor?!

00:10:27.160 --> 00:10:28.960
So, what now?

00:10:28.960 --> 00:10:32.250
Do you really have time
to keep fighting me?

00:10:32.250 --> 00:10:35.920
I'll just finish you off quickly,
then race back to the manor!

00:10:35.920 --> 00:10:37.760
Yes, well...

00:10:37.760 --> 00:10:40.390
I knew you'd say that!

00:10:42.890 --> 00:10:44.350
Where'd that come from?!

00:10:44.350 --> 00:10:46.270
Still, it shouldn't prove fatal.

00:10:46.270 --> 00:10:47.600
It's poisoned.

00:10:50.480 --> 00:10:53.730
We can't have you go on living.

00:10:57.490 --> 00:11:00.530
Since when do royals
use concealed weapons?!

00:11:00.530 --> 00:11:03.910
Even the lowly way of
deception is the high road

00:11:03.910 --> 00:11:07.580
when we royals take it.

00:11:07.580 --> 00:11:11.420
But I didn't actually poison that blade.

00:11:11.420 --> 00:11:12.790
You dirty trickster!

00:11:12.790 --> 00:11:16.380
So, what now? Shall we continue?

00:11:17.380 --> 00:11:18.880
Everyone, fall back!

00:11:18.880 --> 00:11:20.090
We're pulling out!

00:11:20.090 --> 00:11:21.800
Leave them.

00:11:21.800 --> 00:11:23.430
We've other concerns.

00:11:25.220 --> 00:11:29.600
That isn't the cavalry
coming to save us, is it?

00:11:29.600 --> 00:11:32.650
Too bad it's come to this.

00:11:32.650 --> 00:11:37.860
That no-good Grinahae has
broken the agreement we made.

00:11:37.860 --> 00:11:39.320
What now, Your Highness?

00:11:39.320 --> 00:11:41.740
We have no choice. It's time for plan B.

00:11:41.740 --> 00:11:44.120
Which is what?

00:11:44.120 --> 00:11:46.870
Hang our tails between our legs and run!

00:11:51.830 --> 00:11:55.000
We received another sighting
from a checkpoint.

00:11:55.000 --> 00:11:57.340
They broke through only moments ago!

00:11:57.340 --> 00:12:01.760
All right. We'll chase them down
before they can escape into Natra.

00:12:01.760 --> 00:12:06.510
It won't be much of a fight now
that we outnumber them.

00:12:07.970 --> 00:12:09.560
Look! There they are!

00:12:09.560 --> 00:12:11.980
I want the prince alive!

00:12:17.770 --> 00:12:21.740
There's a wide plain
on the other side of this hill.

00:12:21.740 --> 00:12:25.450
That will be the end
of the line for you, Wein!

00:12:25.450 --> 00:12:30.870
Watch me, Geralt, as I apprehend
your killer with my own two hands!

00:12:43.130 --> 00:12:47.260
I'll give negotiations a 50-50 chance
of winning over Grinahae.

00:12:47.260 --> 00:12:50.270
If I fail, we'll hightail it out of town.

00:12:50.270 --> 00:12:52.310
Will you make it back to Natra?

00:12:52.310 --> 00:12:53.810
Probably not.

00:12:53.810 --> 00:12:56.520
Based on horse speed,
checkpoint locations,

00:12:56.520 --> 00:12:58.520
and the lay of the land,

00:12:58.520 --> 00:13:02.440
we should station
our troops on this plain.

00:13:02.440 --> 00:13:06.990
As soon as Grinahae discovers I've fled,
he'll pursue me with his troops.

00:13:06.990 --> 00:13:12.540
But if he focuses on speed, he'll only
be able to bring 100 men at most.

00:13:12.540 --> 00:13:13.910
Right.

00:13:13.910 --> 00:13:15.370
I see what you're doing.

00:13:15.370 --> 00:13:20.000
He'll take just 100 horsemen
from Antgadull's army of 4,000.

00:13:20.000 --> 00:13:24.510
Then we can defeat them
with our much smaller force.

00:13:24.510 --> 00:13:27.510
Grinahae is in for quite a fright!

00:13:27.510 --> 00:13:31.390
He'll believe he is pursuing a
few Natrans with his elite force,

00:13:31.390 --> 00:13:34.310
only to find several hundred
Natran troops waiting.

00:13:34.310 --> 00:13:38.190
Slow down, you two.
It's too early for a victory lap.

00:13:38.190 --> 00:13:39.730
My plan doesn't end there.

00:13:39.730 --> 00:13:43.110
What? Isn't capturing
Grinahae the final blow?

00:13:43.110 --> 00:13:45.610
Nope! Simply capturing him

00:13:45.610 --> 00:13:49.160
may make him more stubborn
and less willing to cooperate.

00:13:49.160 --> 00:13:53.500
Therefore, I have one
more trick up my sleeve.

00:13:56.080 --> 00:13:58.040
Th-This cannot be.

00:13:58.040 --> 00:14:00.460
Milord, we must withdraw at once!

00:14:00.460 --> 00:14:03.130
We'll be safe back at the checkpoint.

00:14:08.930 --> 00:14:11.640
Th-There's a mounted force behind us!

00:14:11.640 --> 00:14:13.890
Whose banner do they carry?!

00:14:13.890 --> 00:14:15.770
Don't tell me it's Natra?!

00:14:15.770 --> 00:14:17.020
Isn't that...

00:14:17.020 --> 00:14:20.730
No! It's the imperial banner!

00:14:20.730 --> 00:14:21.980
Then we're saved!

00:14:21.980 --> 00:14:25.150
I'm a marquess of the empire,
which makes them my ally!

00:14:25.150 --> 00:14:30.160
Let's turn back and rendezvous with them.
Raise our banner and swiftly--

00:14:30.160 --> 00:14:32.580
Milord, please, wait!

00:14:32.580 --> 00:14:35.580
Look at <i>that </i>banner!

00:14:37.750 --> 00:14:41.420
P-Princess Lowellmina's banner?!

00:14:42.710 --> 00:14:45.210
Marquess Antgadull!

00:14:45.210 --> 00:14:49.130
Her Highness, Princess Lowellmina
orders you to accompany us at once!

00:14:49.130 --> 00:14:53.010
Wh-What could... this mean?

00:14:55.430 --> 00:15:00.270
Hell's bells. We must ensure that
such rash action is never repeated.

00:15:00.270 --> 00:15:02.980
Indeed, I am quite aware of that.

00:15:02.980 --> 00:15:07.240
My lord governor, I shall convey
your concern to my brothers.

00:15:07.240 --> 00:15:11.990
I would also have you convey
Your Highness's most tomboyish ways.

00:15:12.950 --> 00:15:16.790
Now then, let us finish off
what we started.

00:15:32.340 --> 00:15:36.810
I, Marquess Antgadull,
am your humble servant.

00:15:36.810 --> 00:15:40.440
I don't understand.
How could it have come to this?

00:15:40.440 --> 00:15:45.070
How shall I ever get out of this?

00:15:45.070 --> 00:15:49.110
Is there not something I could do?!

00:15:51.700 --> 00:15:52.820
--Now, let us begin.

00:15:52.820 --> 00:15:54.120
--Your Imperial Highness!
--Now, let us begin.

00:15:54.120 --> 00:15:57.950
If I may, I would have you
answer but one question!

00:15:57.950 --> 00:16:00.750
Marquess Antgadull!
What insolence is this?!

00:16:00.750 --> 00:16:02.290
It's quite all right.

00:16:02.290 --> 00:16:05.380
Marquess, what would you ask me?

00:16:06.340 --> 00:16:10.760
Why is the Natran prince here?!

00:16:10.760 --> 00:16:13.590
This region belongs to the empire!

00:16:13.590 --> 00:16:18.310
Despite that, the prince
has led a large force here!

00:16:18.310 --> 00:16:22.350
Is this not proof that
he intends to invade?!

00:16:22.350 --> 00:16:24.310
I must condemn Wein!

00:16:24.310 --> 00:16:30.400
She'll be unable to pass judgment upon me
if I prove he has no business being here!

00:16:30.400 --> 00:16:33.110
Of all the things to say.

00:16:33.110 --> 00:16:37.830
Are you here to claim ignorance
of all that transpired?

00:16:37.830 --> 00:16:40.200
I-I don't understand.

00:16:40.200 --> 00:16:44.750
It is only natural that His Highness,
the Prince of Natra, is here.

00:16:44.750 --> 00:16:47.960
After all, the Natran,
imperial, and provincial armies

00:16:47.960 --> 00:16:50.800
are launching a joint military exercise.

00:16:54.800 --> 00:16:58.560
The joint exercise
should be underway by now.

00:16:58.560 --> 00:16:59.810
Yes.

00:16:59.810 --> 00:17:04.060
The respective armies should be present
if all has proceeded as planned.

00:17:04.060 --> 00:17:08.360
Ambassador Tallum, we cannot
thank you enough for your tireless effort.

00:17:08.360 --> 00:17:09.900
Think nothing of it.

00:17:09.900 --> 00:17:12.610
I merely wished for the
prince and princess to meet.

00:17:12.610 --> 00:17:15.030
What a shame it would be

00:17:15.030 --> 00:17:19.580
if Lord Geralt's unfortunate
demise brought it all to naught.

00:17:19.580 --> 00:17:22.580
Acting as an intermediary
with the governor of Gairan

00:17:22.580 --> 00:17:25.710
was but a simple matter
for an ambassador such as me.

00:17:25.710 --> 00:17:27.750
That's most reassuring.

00:17:28.920 --> 00:17:31.300
A joint military exercise?

00:17:31.300 --> 00:17:34.050
I don't believe what I hear.

00:17:34.050 --> 00:17:39.350
Does this mean Wein had everything
planned by the time of his visit?

00:17:39.350 --> 00:17:42.220
He hoped to persuade me if possible,

00:17:42.220 --> 00:17:44.480
and failing that, he would flee here

00:17:44.480 --> 00:17:47.940
and trap me between the
Natran and provincial armies.

00:17:47.940 --> 00:17:52.820
He even brought the armies together
under the pretext of a joint exercise.

00:17:52.820 --> 00:17:54.740
How could this be?

00:17:54.740 --> 00:17:57.860
How could this have happened to me?

00:17:57.860 --> 00:17:59.280
Careful, now.

00:18:00.330 --> 00:18:04.660
It would appear that you are unwell.

00:18:06.290 --> 00:18:11.540
No matter what I do, I cannot win.

00:18:11.540 --> 00:18:15.970
Tell me, my lord, what will you do now?

00:18:15.970 --> 00:18:18.180
What will I do?

00:18:18.180 --> 00:18:22.600
It matters not to me.

00:18:22.600 --> 00:18:26.270
She wishes me to choose
between life and death.

00:18:28.480 --> 00:18:31.400
I-I...

00:18:34.360 --> 00:18:35.900
Please...

00:18:35.900 --> 00:18:39.030
I beg Your Imperial Highness's mercy,

00:18:39.030 --> 00:18:43.700
though I know I am not
worthy of your favor.

00:18:48.210 --> 00:18:51.000
I must say farewell for now.

00:18:51.000 --> 00:18:55.260
There were many twists and turns,
but you and Wein saved me.

00:18:55.260 --> 00:18:57.130
And for that, I thank you.

00:18:57.130 --> 00:18:59.340
There's no need to thank us.

00:18:59.340 --> 00:19:01.930
What I want to know, Lowa, is it true?

00:19:01.930 --> 00:19:03.350
Is what true?

00:19:03.350 --> 00:19:07.480
That you've called off the
proposed marriage with Wein.

00:19:07.480 --> 00:19:08.890
It's true.

00:19:08.890 --> 00:19:12.110
If I'm to extend the empire's influence,

00:19:12.110 --> 00:19:15.860
it is better to remain unwed
than marry foreign royalty.

00:19:15.860 --> 00:19:18.030
It won't seem unnatural if I call it off

00:19:18.030 --> 00:19:20.950
due to potential instability
in the empire.

00:19:20.950 --> 00:19:24.660
But, Lowa, you do like Wein, don't you?

00:19:26.580 --> 00:19:30.210
W-Well, I suppose you
could say I like him as a friend.

00:19:30.210 --> 00:19:32.250
I mean as a woman.

00:19:32.250 --> 00:19:35.590
Wh-Whatever do you mean?

00:19:35.590 --> 00:19:39.670
Why would I like such an eccentric?

00:19:39.670 --> 00:19:41.260
Where did you hear that?

00:19:41.260 --> 00:19:46.390
First, put your cup down
before you stain your clothes.

00:19:47.220 --> 00:19:49.430
How long have you known?

00:19:49.430 --> 00:19:51.520
Ever since the academy.

00:19:51.520 --> 00:19:54.400
Was I really such an open book?!

00:19:54.400 --> 00:19:55.820
Pretty much.

00:20:00.150 --> 00:20:03.410
Very well, I'll come clean.

00:20:03.410 --> 00:20:06.370
I do have feelings for him.

00:20:06.370 --> 00:20:09.750
But it's okay that the
proposed marriage didn't work out.

00:20:09.750 --> 00:20:11.830
As imperial princess?

00:20:11.830 --> 00:20:13.250
Yes, there's that.

00:20:13.250 --> 00:20:15.500
However...

00:20:15.500 --> 00:20:17.000
That's all right.

00:20:17.000 --> 00:20:20.170
Some feelings are hard to express.

00:20:23.550 --> 00:20:26.550
Now that we've obtained proof
of the rebellion plot,

00:20:26.550 --> 00:20:28.970
it seems everything will be sorted out.

00:20:28.970 --> 00:20:30.520
So it seems.

00:20:30.520 --> 00:20:33.600
I had fun. It's been ages
since we schemed like that.

00:20:33.600 --> 00:20:36.610
I mean, did you see Grinahae's face?

00:20:38.230 --> 00:20:43.320
But why go that far? Didn't you
have other means at your disposal?

00:20:43.320 --> 00:20:44.360
Like what?

00:20:44.360 --> 00:20:48.330
For instance, have one of
your spies assassinate Geralt.

00:20:48.330 --> 00:20:52.120
That way, the honor of Grinahae's son
would've remained intact,

00:20:52.120 --> 00:20:54.420
and he'd be easier to reason with.

00:20:54.420 --> 00:20:58.880
Or you could have abducted Grinahae
and tortured him till he confessed.

00:20:58.880 --> 00:21:03.010
I did think along those lines.

00:21:03.010 --> 00:21:08.720
But I figured if I could break him,
he would be easier for you to control.

00:21:09.760 --> 00:21:12.930
You did that for me?

00:21:12.930 --> 00:21:15.400
Well, I <i>did </i>make a promise.

00:21:15.400 --> 00:21:20.280
If I fail to escape whatever mess you
drag me into, I might help out a bit.

00:21:23.110 --> 00:21:27.780
Anyway, I've done all I can.

00:21:27.780 --> 00:21:30.160
You take it from here,

00:21:30.160 --> 00:21:32.750
miss empress-to-be!

00:21:32.750 --> 00:21:34.790
Yes, I've got this.

00:21:35.580 --> 00:21:38.080
He remembered his promise.

00:21:46.510 --> 00:21:50.930
But Lowa, you do like Wein, don't you?

00:21:50.930 --> 00:21:54.560
Ninym, it goes without
saying that I like Wein.

00:21:54.560 --> 00:22:00.610
But what I really long for is
the relationship you have with him.

00:22:00.610 --> 00:22:04.530
He's a royal, and you're from a people
who are discriminated against.

00:22:04.530 --> 00:22:07.160
You're from two different worlds.

00:22:07.160 --> 00:22:10.450
I've always longed for someone like that,

00:22:10.450 --> 00:22:14.000
someone I can trust
as much as they trust me.

00:22:14.000 --> 00:22:19.460
I've often thought about how
I'd love to be included in that.

00:22:19.460 --> 00:22:24.170
But now I realize
I don't yet have what it takes.

00:22:26.880 --> 00:22:28.470
That's why

00:22:28.470 --> 00:22:31.180
I <i>will </i>become empress

00:22:31.180 --> 00:22:36.390
so that I can proudly stand
alongside both of you one day.
